Plain-English Summary

You may generally:

* download the Software;
* install it;
* use it personally;
* use it for hobbies and learning;
* inspect the source code;
* evaluate it;
* link other people to the official project.

Without additional permission, you may generally not:

* sell it;
* use it commercially;
* use it as part of a business operation;
* charge people to access it;
* turn it into a SaaS or paid service;
* modify and redistribute it;
* publish your own altered version;
* repackage it;
* incorporate substantial parts into another commercial product;
* remove copyright or licence notices;
* claim authorship;
* use substantial portions as AI/model-training material;
* distribute unofficial copies.

Public availability does not mean that the Software is public domain or open source.

The copyright holder retains ownership and all rights not expressly granted.

This summary is explanatory only. The full licence controls if there is any inconsistency.